4. Your building has an industrial past
The building dates to 1915 and formerly housed the Mica Insulator Company. That company was founded in 1893 by engineers associated with the Edison Machine Works. The large industrial interiors and windows made the property suitable for conversion to housing.
Schenectady Metroplex Development Authority
It was redeveloped into 845 Commons, which officially opened in January 2015. The YMCA describes the project as an eight-year, $26.5 million undertaking and the largest single-site supportive-housing residence west of the Hudson.
Capital District YMCA
So your home has passed through at least three distinct roles: industrial workplace, disused factory, and residential community.
